quiz 4 | What's an isotope?
* Atoms of the same element with different numbers of neutrons
o Atoms with different numbers of protons
o A charged atom
o A molecule of two elements
= A charged atom is an ion.
> Next

quiz 4 | What type of bond holds the two strands of DNA together?
* Hydrogen bonds
o Ionic bonds
o Metallic bonds
o Covalent bonds only
= Weak enough to unzip for copying.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which element is the basis of organic chemistry?
* Carbon
o Oxygen
o Nitrogen
o Hydrogen
= Carbon forms four bonds and long chains.
> Next

quiz 4 | What does a catalyst do?
* Speeds up a reaction without being consumed
o Stops a reaction
o Provides energy for a reaction
o Becomes a product
= It lowers the activation energy.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which noble gas glows red-orange in signs?
* Neon
o Argon
o Helium
o Xenon
= Other colours come from other gases or coated tubes.
