quiz 3 | Which law says pressure × volume is constant at fixed temperature?
* Boyle's law
o Charles's law
o Hooke's law
o Ohm's law
= Charles's law relates volume and temperature.
> Next

quiz 3 | Hooke's law states…
* Force is proportional to extension (F = kx)
o Energy equals mass times c²
o Pressure equals force over area
o Current equals voltage over resistance
= Up to the elastic limit.
> Next

quiz 3 | What type of wave is sound in air?
* Longitudinal
o Transverse
o Electromagnetic
o Standing only
= Air molecules oscillate along the direction of travel.
